.TH HTTP_INIT 3
.SH NAME
http_init \- prepare an HTTP client structure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "void http_init(http* " h ", const char* " host ", uint16 " port ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_init ()
clears the structure
.I h
and sets the defaults: no socket (sock is -1), non-blocking mode, no keep-alive, no TLS,
HTTP/1.0 for a GET. If
.I host
is not 0 it is copied into
.IR h->host ,
.I port
is stored in
.IR h->port .
Both are replaced when a request is started with a URL by
.BR http_open (3),
so calling it with 0 and 0 is the usual thing.
.P
Fields can be changed afterwards, before the request is started:
.I version
(11 for HTTP/1.1),
.I keepalive,
.I nonblocking
and
.IR stream .
The structure must not hold resources of an earlier use; release them with
.BR http_close (3)
and
.BR http_free (3)
first.
.SH SEE ALSO
http(3), http_open(3), http_free(3)
